pos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-08-13T08:27:30Z","updated_at":"2024-08-13T08:27:30Z","body":"This is amazing, I was not expecting such a prompt response. The usage as a pure mirror is mostly to simplify the reproduction code to the bare minimum, nevertheless we might introduce the usage of `synonym` for some of our use cases. Also we definitely stretch or even abuse the sqlalchemy beyond the regular use cases.\r\n\r\nThe 1.4 backport is not critical for us to move forward and still it is just a temporary phase in moving towards 2.1. It shouldn't be hard to prevent triggering of the issue by some code changes on our side or by monkey patching your fix.\r\n\r\nIt took quite some time to isolate the issue doing code diving in the internals and I was wondering if the fix would happen in a similar manner how you actually did in AnnotatedColumnElement.\r\n\r\n@zzzeek, thanks for all the work on sqlalchemy!\r\n \r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/2285664069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"tomas-sk","id":23239606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjM5NjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23239606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk","html_url":"https://github.com/tomas-sk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomas-sk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subs